From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:13:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Keep section flags when copying, so the RELRO segment
 survives

libr created every output section with the input's flags plus
SEC_LINKER_CREATED. bfd copies the input's program headers only while
every section inside a segment keeps its flags (copy_private_bfd_data
in bfd/elf.c). Otherwise it rebuilds them, and the rebuild drops
PT_GNU_RELRO (rewrite_elf_program_header). So every file libr wrote
lost its RELRO segment. Because tdelfeditor runs on every binary and
library TDE builds, no TDE binary has RELRO, although the linker was
asked for it:

    readelf -lW /opt/trinity/bin/konsole | grep -c GNU_RELRO    # 0
    readelf -lW /usr/bin/ls | grep -c GNU_RELRO                 # 1

objcopy, over the same libbfd, keeps the segment. It also drops it once
the flags of a section inside a segment are changed, and keeps it when
the changed section lies in no segment.

Create the output sections with the input's flags exactly. That is what
objcopy does, and what was already done for .ARM.attributes, whose
section type the extra flag also lost.

Tested with binutils 2.44 on an executable, a PIE, a shared library and
a TDE binary carrying libr resources, both clearing and writing a
resource. Each output keeps GNU_RELRO, the program headers and section
table match the input apart from the resource section, written
resources read back, and the programs run or load.
---
 src/libr-bfd.c | 20 +++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libr-bfd.c b/src/libr-bfd.c
index b472543..f4e46b9 100644
--- a/src/libr-bfd.c
+++ b/src/libr-bfd.c
@@ -180,19 +180,13 @@ int setup_sections(bfd *ihandle, bfd *ohandle)
 		{
 			continue; /* Section has been marked for deletion */
 		}
-		/* Use SEC_LINKER_CREATED to ask the libbfd backend to take care of configuring the section */
-
-		// Keep the ARM_ATTRIBUTES section type intact on armhf systems
-		// If this is not done, readelf -A will not print any architecture information for the modified library,
-		// and ldd will report that the library cannot be found
-		if (strcmp(iscn->name, ".ARM.attributes") == 0)
-		{
-			oscn = bfd_make_section_anyway_with_flags(ohandle, iscn->name, iscn->flags);
-		}
-		else
-		{
-			oscn = bfd_make_section_anyway_with_flags(ohandle, iscn->name, iscn->flags | SEC_LINKER_CREATED);
-		}
+		/* Keep the input's flags exactly. bfd copies the input's program
+		 * headers only while every section inside a segment keeps its
+		 * flags; otherwise it rebuilds them, and the rebuild drops
+		 * PT_GNU_RELRO. Adding SEC_LINKER_CREATED here stripped RELRO
+		 * from every file libr wrote, and lost .ARM.attributes' section
+		 * type on armhf, which is why that section was once exempted. */
+		oscn = bfd_make_section_anyway_with_flags(ohandle, iscn->name, iscn->flags);
 		if(oscn == NULL)
 		{
 			printf("failed to create out section: %s\n", bfd_errmsg(bfd_get_error()));
